.TH FSEEK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fseek \- reposition a Crunch file stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int fseek(struct FILE* " stream ", long " offset ", int " whence ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Repositions the stream by a signed byte offset relative to
.BR SEEK_SET ,
.BR SEEK_CUR ,
or
.BR SEEK_END .
On success the stream's end-of-file indicator is cleared; its error indicator
is unchanged.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or \-1 with
.B errno
set on failure. A null stream fails with
.BR EINVAL .
Nonseekable streams can fail with
.BR ESPIPE .
.SH NOTES
Streams are unbuffered. On update streams, follow the C rules for positioning
between reading and writing. Crunch streams are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fopen (3crunch),
.BR ftell (3crunch),
.BR rewind (3crunch),
.BR feof (3crunch),
.BR ferror (3crunch),
.BR fread (3crunch),
.BR fwrite (3crunch),
.BR lseek (3crunch)
